            <ArticleTitle>Opioid-induced itching: morphine sulfate and hydromorphone hydrochloride.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of severe morphine-induced itch unrelieved by antihistamines, which responded to a change to hydromorphone. The possible mechanisms of opioid-induced itch are briefly discussed. It is unclear if it is due to histamine release, an opioid-receptor mediated effect, or idiosyncratic drug reaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
